      "content": "exactly. and if they're collecting gait and heart rate, they don't even need my permission to know my stress levels or if i'm anxious/depressed just by how i walk. it feels like they're building a way to predict my mood before i even know it myself. don't you think the technical capability alone makes this a massive, unaddressed security risk? like, isn't it basically a covert way to harvest psychological data under the guise of \"fitness\"?",
